  "published": "2026-11-26T20:59:25.037Z",
  "releaseNotes": "10.11.2: the 10.11.1 change, versioned together with the other packages so it can be published (10.11.1 never reached nuget.org). 10.11.1: AddServiceFabricReadiness() also marks 404s with X-ServiceFabric: ResourceNotFound, so the reverse proxy stops retrying the 404s of hosts built by hand such as Online.Payments (Eternet/Devs.Issues#2852, #2859). 10.11.0: in Service Fabric an API that answers a caller without a session with anything but 401 or 403 (a sign-in redirect or an HTML page) keeps the instance from getting ready; one synthetic challenge per authentication scheme that protects an API endpoint, browser-only schemes listed under Eternet:BrowserSignInSchemes (Eternet/Devs.Issues#2824, #2825). 10.10.0 (never published, its changes ship in 10.11.0): StartHostedServicesWhenReady(): the application's background services start once the instance reported ready, used by database readiness (Eternet/Devs.Issues#2823). In Service Fabric an empty key, password, secret, token or connection string keeps the instance from getting ready unless Eternet:OptionalSettings gives the reason (Eternet/Devs.Issues#2817). A Blazor render batch that the browser rejects because its page no longer matches the circuit (no renderer, no element for a component, or a null parent on removeChild/insertBefore) is logged as Warning instead of Error in centralized logs (Eternet/Devs.Issues#2748, #2751, #2752). JavaScript interop failures and any other circuit exception keep Error.",
